  "answer": "This has been reported before. In PowerToys#48858 (v0.100.1), the Dock performance stats don't remember the adapter chosen with right-click → Next Network after a restart. Several other users there confirm it. PowerToys#47765 and PowerToys#48954 ask for the same thing: remember the network or GPU choice across restarts. The archive has no fix or official workaround for the adapter choice. For now, either re-select your Wi-Fi adapter with Next Network after each boot, or disable the unused Ethernet adapter, which is what one user in #48858 did. Add your details and your bug report ZIP to #48858 so the team can track it. A related bug, #48224, was a different Performance Monitor setting (the network speed unit) being wiped from settings.json. It is not confirmed as the cause of your problem."
 },
